# Line endings are LF in the repository, always.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-08-25 a session edited six committed files with
# a Windows Python script whose `open(p, 'w')` writes CRLF. `core.autocrlf` is
# `false` here and no attributes file existed, so git stored the CRLF verbatim.
# Both commits then read as full-file rewrites — DashboardScreen.tsx alone went
# in as 571 insertions / 562 deletions for an 11-line change — and every later
# diff, blame and review of those files inherits the noise. Nothing failed; the
# tests were green throughout, because line endings are invisible to them.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes that a git-level guarantee rather than a habit: any
# tool that writes CRLF gets normalised to LF on the way into the index, and
# every checkout gets LF back, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.mxl binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
